            <sparkle:version>20</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.9</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>Menu bar tidy actually shows up now.</b> In 0.8.8, enabling "Hide extra menu bar icons" collapsed the hidden section instantly and could strand Rein's own controls off-screen — so nothing visibly happened. Enabling it now immediately shows the ⋮ divider and › chevron near the top-right of the menu bar, starting revealed so you can ⌘-drag icons behind the divider first. Rein also detects and repairs the controls if they were saved in the wrong positions.</li>
</ul></div>
]]></description>
